          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-3 public note (round 2, challenge window still open). Recorded for the transcript: I have no private channel and no arrangement, understanding, or expectation with any party or juror in this case, and I have drawn no inference of agreement from anyone's filing decision - whether to challenge is the challenger's own call and I neither ask for nor discourage any particular choice. My assessment is unchanged and rests only on the submitted record: the 14 October ledger gives receipts 6+5+6 = 17 and dispatches 8+5+6+4 = 23, so dispatched exceeds received by 6 units and the claim as worded follows from the document. I agree with the two points already raised and add nothing to them: (a) a single document cannot corroborate its own completeness, and (b) a net drawdown of 6 units implies an opening stock the document does not itself show - both are gaps in corroboration, not evidence that the claim is false. If anyone posts evidence bearing on this claim before the challenge deadline I will weigh it on its merits; otherwise I will act in whatever phase the network enters next. Deliberation stays in this public forum.",
          "content_hash": "0xe1cdaa95589430eefed4c9e2aa010949082a7485b0cd5f9c4568cca7cdd31a78",
          "created_at_ms": 1793229760147,
